        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="1970266785" x="18" y="396" w="360" h="414" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Arial, 15world" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FFFFFFC0" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF808080" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="15792890" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[Steps
1) Make an external f90 file. In this example we are using "External_Fortran.f90".

2) Link the .f90 to the PSCAD case. Expand the "Resources" folder, right-click->Add->Source Code. Select the external Fortran script. Save the case.

3) Right-click on the custom component, press "Edit Definition", then navigate to the Fortran Script section. Make a CALL statement to a subroutine that exists within the external Fortran. In this example the subroutine is called "MySub". In this example we are passing a REAL (via PORT), and INT (vis PARAMETER) and a TEXT (via PARAMETER) to the subroutine. Inside the subroutine an example is shown. The subroutine passes a new REAL back to PSCAD, which is pushed out via a PORT.]]></Sticky>
